ocean/diag_table

ls -l diag_table --> diagnostic_profiles/diag_table_standard (that means out of all of the other files, the main one 'diag_table' is hyperlinked with the diag_table_standard

but have to do a few steps to make edits:
  1. Go to folder
      cd /scratch/lo70/sd3017/access-esm/3.fsurf/trial22_restart60/ocean/diagnostic_profiles/source_yaml_files
  2. Copy the hyperlinked standard one to the name the script expects (the script only reads a file called exactly diag_table_source.yaml in the folder you run in from)
      cp diag_table_standard_source.yaml diag_table_source.yaml
  3. Edit your new copy
      vim diag_table_source.yaml 
      
        e.g. putting # to comment out variables that aren't needed

        also adding daily fields (copied the format from a previous list, and then added surface_temp and surface_salt)
            'daily 2d ocean fields':
        defaults:  # these can be overridden for individual fields below
            file_name_dimension: 2d  # descriptor for filename, e.g. 3d, 2d, scalar
            output_freq: 1  # integer: output sampling frequency in output_freq_units (0: every timestep; -1: only at end of run)
            output_freq_units: days  # time units for output: years, months, days, hours, minutes, or seconds
        fields:
            surface_temp:
            surface_salt:

    4. Generate/Write the new diag_table
    python3 make_diag_table.py

    5. Move it up and give it a clear name
    mv diag_table ../diag_table_mine

    6. Point the symlink at it
    ln -sf diagnostic_profiles/diag_table_mine diag_table
    ls -l ocean/diag_table (so now you should see diag_table --> diagnostic_profiles/diag_table_mine)



